Q: Prevent line/paragraph breaks in contentEditable A: <p><strong>Including if you copy &amp; paste something with line breaks.</strong></p>
<p>You can do this in a single line of HTML:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div 
  contenteditable=&quot;true&quot; 
  onkeydown=&quot;return event.key != 'Enter';&quot;
  onpaste=&quot;event.preventDefault(); document.execCommand('insertText', false, event.clipboardData.getData('text').replace(/\n/g, ''))&quot;
&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If the user presses enter, ignore it. If they pasted something with line breaks, remove them.</p>
<p>Here's a working example:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="true" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code snippet-currently-hidden">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>div {
  cursor: text;
  font-family: 'Calibri';
  border: 1px solid black;
  padding: 4px;

  &amp;:not(:focus):empty::before {
    opacity: 0.5;
    pointer-events: none;
    content: attr(placeholder);
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div 
  placeholder="Type here..."
  contenteditable="true" 
  onkeydown="return event.key != 'Enter';"
  onpaste="event.preventDefault(); document.execCommand('insertText', false, event.clipboardData.getData('text').replace(/\n/g, ''))"
&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
